    <main id="main-content" class="static-main">
      <article class="px-5 pt-12 pb-6 lg:px-8 lg:pt-24 lg:pb-16 max-w-[1600px] mx-auto">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-3 mb-4">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-brand-500/20 text-brand-200 uppercase tracking-wide">Chapter 3</span>
          <span class="h-px flex-1 bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-500/30 to-transparent"></span>
        </div>

        <h1 class="section-title text-3xl tracking-tight leading-tight lg:text-5xl">How Blockchain Works</h1>
        <p class="mt-2.5 text-[15px] lg:mt-4 lg:text-xl text-brand-200">Understanding the process of adding blocks to the chain</p>

        <section class="mt-8 lg:mt-12 reveal" id="introduction">
          <div class="glass-panel p-6 lg:p-8">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold lg:text-3xl lesson-heading">Introduction</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed text-[15px] lg:text-base">
              A blockchain does not update itself. It requires a process — a series of steps that computers on the network follow to add new information. Think of it like a classroom where every student has the same notebook. When someone wants to add a new page, they must announce it to the class, and everyone must agree the page is valid before it gets bound into the notebook.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed text-[15px] lg:text-base">
              This process is what makes blockchain trustworthy. No single person can secretly add or change pages without everyone else noticing.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed text-[15px] lg:text-base">
              In this chapter, you will learn the step-by-step process of how a blockchain processes transactions, creates new blocks, and maintains a permanent, tamper-proof record.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-6 lg:mt-10 reveal" id="how-it-works">
          <div class="glass-panel p-6 lg:p-8">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold lg:text-3xl lesson-heading">How It Works</h2>

            <div class="mt-4 p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.03] border border-brand-500/10">
              <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">Nodes in the network monitor incoming transaction <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('broadcast')">broadcasts</span>. When a transaction is validated, miners bundle it into a block, compute the cryptographic <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('hash')">hash</span> linking it to the previous block, and <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('append')">append</span> it to their copy of the ledger.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="mt-5 p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.03] border border-brand-500/10">
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-200 mb-3">Everyday Object Analogy</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">Think of the blockchain process like adding a page to a shared yearbook. First, someone writes an entry (transaction). Then, the yearbook committee (nodes) checks that the entry is appropriate. Once approved, the page is sealed with a unique stamp (<span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('hash')">hash</span>) and glued to the previous page. Anyone can see that the seal matches, proving the page has not been swapped.</p>
            </div>

            <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-display font-bold lg:text-2xl">The Four-Step Process</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed text-[15px] lg:text-base">
              Every blockchain transaction follows the same sequence:
            </p>
            <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl text-center border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-6 h-6 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M15 15l-2 5L9 9l11 4-5 2zm0 0l5 5M7.188 2.239l.777 2.897M5.136 7.965l-2.898-.777M13.95 4.05l-2.122 2.122m-5.657 5.656l-2.12 2.122"/></svg>
                </div>
                <h4 class="font-display font-semibold text-base text-brand-200">1. Transaction Created</h4>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-theme-muted">A user signs a transaction with their private key and <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('broadcast')">broadcasts</span> it to the network.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl text-center border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-6 h-6 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z"/></svg>
                </div>
                <h4 class="font-display font-semibold text-base text-brand-200">2. Validation</h4>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-theme-muted">Network nodes verify the signature, check balances, and confirm the transaction is valid.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl text-center border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-6 h-6 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M19 11H5m14 0a2 2 0 012 2v6a2 2 0 01-2 2H5a2 2 0 01-2-2v-6a2 2 0 012-2m14 0V9a2 2 0 00-2-2M5 11V9a2 2 0 012-2m0 0V5a2 2 0 012-2h6a2 2 0 012 2v2M7 7h10"/></svg>
                </div>
                <h4 class="font-display font-semibold text-base text-brand-200">3. Block Formation</h4>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-theme-muted">Valid transactions are bundled into a block with the previous block's <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('hash')">hash</span>.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl text-center border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-12 h-12 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mx-auto mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-6 h-6 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"/></svg>
                </div>
                <h4 class="font-display font-semibold text-base text-brand-200">4. <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('consensus')">Consensus</span> & Addition</h4>
                <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-theme-muted">The network reaches <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('consensus')">consensus</span>, and the new block is added to every node's copy of the chain.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-display font-bold lg:text-2xl">How Blocks Are Linked</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed text-[15px] lg:text-base">
              Each block contains a <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('hash')">hash</span> of the previous block's header. This creates a chain:
            </p>
            <div class="mt-5 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
              <div class="glass-panel p-4 rounded-xl border border-brand-500/10">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-200 mb-1">Block 1 (<span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('genesis-block')">Genesis</span>)</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">Index 0, data: "First block", <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('hash')">Hash</span>: 0x4f3a... (no previous <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('hash')">hash</span>)</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-4 rounded-xl border border-brand-500/10">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-200 mb-1">Block 2</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">Index 1, data: "Transaction A", <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('hash')">Hash</span>: 0x8b2d..., Prev: 0x4f3a...</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-4 rounded-xl border border-brand-500/10">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-200 mb-1">Block 3</p>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">Index 2, data: "Transaction B", <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('hash')">Hash</span>: 0xc7e1..., Prev: 0x8b2d...</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <h3 class="mt-8 text-xl font-display font-bold lg:text-2xl">Deeper Dive</h3>
            <p class="mt-3 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed text-[15px] lg:text-base">
              This structure ensures immutability. If an attacker edits Block 2, its <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('hash')">hash</span> changes. Since Block 3 contains the old <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('hash')">hash</span> of Block 2, the link breaks. The entire subsequent chain becomes invalid, alerting other nodes to reject the edit.
            </p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed text-[15px] lg:text-base">
              In Proof of Work systems, <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('mining')">mining</span> the block requires solving a computational puzzle — finding a '<span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('nonce')">nonce</span>' value that, when hashed with the block header, produces a <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('hash')">hash</span> with a target number of leading zeros. This process is energy-intensive by design, making it economically impractical to attack the network.
            </p>

            <div class="mt-5 p-4 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.03] border border-brand-500/10">
              <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-brand-200 mb-2">Key Insight</p>
              <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">Blockchain is not instantaneous. Adding a new block to Bitcoin takes about 10 minutes on average. This deliberate slowness is what makes the system secure — speed is sacrificed for safety.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-6 lg:mt-10 reveal" id="vocabulary">
          <div class="glass-panel p-6 lg:p-8">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold lg:text-3xl lesson-heading">Vocabulary Table</h2>
            <div class="mt-4 overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="vocab-table w-full text-sm">
                <thead>
                  <tr>
                    <th class="text-theme">Term</th>
                    <th class="text-theme">Definition</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody class="text-theme-muted">
                  <tr id="vocab-mining"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('mining')">Mining</span></td><td>The process of validating transactions and adding new blocks to the blockchain.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-nonce"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('nonce')">Nonce</span></td><td>A random number miners adjust to produce a valid block hash.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-hash"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('hash')">Hash</span></td><td>A fixed-length string generated from input data, acting as a unique digital fingerprint.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-genesis-block"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('genesis-block')">Genesis Block</span></td><td>The very first block in a blockchain, with no previous hash.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-consensus"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('consensus')">Consensus</span></td><td>An agreement protocol among distributed nodes to accept a new block.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-broadcast"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('broadcast')">Broadcast</span></td><td>Sending a transaction or block to all nodes on the network.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-validate"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('validate')">Validate</span></td><td>To check that a transaction or block follows the network's rules.</td></tr>
                  <tr id="vocab-append"><td><span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('append')">Append</span></td><td>To add a new block to the end of the existing blockchain.</td></tr>
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-6 lg:mt-10 reveal" id="fun-facts">
          <div class="glass-panel p-6 lg:p-8">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold lg:text-3xl lesson-heading">Fun Facts</h2>
            <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.02] border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"/></svg>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">Bitcoin adds a new block approximately every 10 minutes — regardless of how many transactions are waiting.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.02] border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"/></svg>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">Changing a single letter in a block changes its <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('hash')">hash</span> output completely — this is called the avalanche effect.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.02] border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"/></svg>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">The Bitcoin blockchain is over 500 gigabytes in size and growing every day.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.02] border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"/></svg>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">If you lost your private key, you can never access your cryptocurrency — there is no "forgot password" option on a blockchain.</p>
              </div>
              <div class="glass-panel p-5 rounded-xl bg-brand-500/[0.02] border border-brand-500/10">
                <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-brand-500/10 flex items-center justify-center mb-3">
                  <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-brand-300" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5"><path d="M13 10V3L4 14h7v7l9-11h-7z"/></svg>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm text-theme-muted">The very first block of the Bitcoin blockchain, called the <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('genesis-block')">Genesis Block</span>, contains a hidden message: "The Times 03/Jan/2009 Chancellor on brink of second bailout for banks."</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- Interactive Diagram -->
        <section class="mt-6 lg:mt-10 reveal" id="interactive-diagram">
          <div class="glass-panel p-6 lg:p-8 text-center">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold lg:text-3xl lesson-heading">Interactive Diagram</h2>
            <p class="mt-4 text-theme-muted">Launch the interactive diagram to see this in action.</p>
            <a href="diagrams/diagram-03-problems-with-tradit/index.html" class="btn-primary magnetic-btn inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm py-3 px-6 mt-4" aria-label="Open interactive diagram">
              Open Interactive Diagram
              <svg class="w-4 h-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg>
            </a>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="mt-6 lg:mt-10 reveal" id="knowledge-check">
          <div class="glass-panel p-6 lg:p-8">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold lg:text-3xl lesson-heading">Knowledge Check</h2>

            <div class="mt-6 space-y-6">

              <div class="kb-check">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-theme">1. What happens if a historical block's data is edited?</p>
                <div class="mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm text-theme-muted">
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq1" class="accent-brand-500"> The database runs faster</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq1" class="accent-brand-500"> Subsequent block <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('hash')">hash</span> links break</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq1" class="accent-brand-500"> The domain name resolves</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq1" class="accent-brand-500"> The CPU clock cycles multiply</label>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-green-400 kb-answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Subsequent block <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('hash')">hash</span> links break</p>
              </div>

              <div class="kb-check">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-theme">2. What is the role of a '<span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('nonce')">nonce</span>' in <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('mining')">mining</span>?</p>
                <div class="mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm text-theme-muted">
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq2" class="accent-brand-500"> It stores the transaction data</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq2" class="accent-brand-500"> It is a random number adjusted to create a valid <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('hash')">hash</span></label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq2" class="accent-brand-500"> It identifies the sender of a transaction</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq2" class="accent-brand-500"> It encrypts the block data</label>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-green-400 kb-answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> It is a random number adjusted to create a valid <span class="vocab cursor-pointer" onclick="scrollToVocabulary('hash')">hash</span></p>
              </div>

              <div class="kb-check">
                <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-theme">3. Approximately how often does Bitcoin add a new block to its chain?</p>
                <div class="mt-2 space-y-2 text-sm text-theme-muted">
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq3" class="accent-brand-500"> Every 10 seconds</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq3" class="accent-brand-500"> Every 10 minutes</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq3" class="accent-brand-500"> Every 10 hours</label>
                  <label class="flex items-center gap-2 cursor-pointer"><input type="radio" name="mcq3" class="accent-brand-500"> Every 10 days</label>
                </div>
                <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-green-400 kb-answer"><strong>Answer:</strong> Every 10 minutes</p>
              </div>

            </div>

            <div class="mt-6 text-center">
              <button type="button" id="reveal-answers-btn" class="btn-primary magnetic-btn text-sm py-2.5 px-6">Show Answers</button>
            </div>

            <script>
              (function() {
                var btn = document.getElementById('reveal-answers-btn');
                if (btn) {
                  btn.addEventListener('click', function() {
                    var answers = document.querySelectorAll('.kb-answer');
                    var hidden = false;
                    answers.forEach(function(a) {
                      if (!a.classList.contains('revealed')) hidden = true;
                    });
                    answers.forEach(function(a) {
                      a.classList.toggle('revealed', hidden);
                    });
                    btn.textContent = hidden ? 'Hide Answers' : 'Show Answers';
                  });
                }
              })();
            </script>
          </div>
        </section>

